desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Ocamllint Filenameconcat"
	title_zh: "Ocamllint Filenameconcat"
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-ocamllint-filenameconcat"
	risk: "Security"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `ocamllint-filenameconcat` (ocaml/lang/security/filenameconcat.yaml).
Original message: When attacker supplied data is passed to Filename.concat directory traversal attacks might be possible.
CWE: CWE-35: Path Traversal
References:
- https://v2.ocaml.org/api/Filename.html
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal Semgrep pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.ml": <<<POS
Filename.concat
POS
	"safefile://pos.ml": <<<NEG
Filename.quote_command
NEG
)

${*.ml}.pattern_regex(/(?:Filename\.concat)/) as $p0
${*.mli}.pattern_regex(/(?:Filename\.concat)/) as $p1
$p0 + $p1 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Ocamllint Filenameconcat",
	title_zh: "Ocamllint Filenameconcat",
	message: "Ocamllint Filenameconcat detected.",
}
